<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!--
    Notarising a build means signing it with the hardened runtime, and the
    hardened runtime refuses the microphone to an app that has not asked for
    it here. Info.plist says the sentence the system shows; this says the app
    is allowed to be asked about at all, and without it the prompt never
    appears and recording fails with no reason given.

    Parlour records in ffmpeg rather than in this process, but the child is
    not the process the system asks about: the permission is attributed to
    the app that started it, so the entitlement belongs here too.
  -->
  <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
